                {
                  "id": "h-signs-need-repair",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Signs Your Truck May Need Diesel Exhaust System Repair",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "signs-need-repair"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-need-repair-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "In addition to DEF warnings, there are several signs your truck may need professional service. Common symptoms include:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-signs-need-repair-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Check engine lights"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Excessive exhaust smoke"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Loss of power"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Frequent regeneration cycles"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Poor fuel economy"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Trouble accelerating"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Fault codes related to emissions systems"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-need-repair-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "These issues can sometimes overlap with problems involving diesel fuel system parts, sensors, or engine performance components, which is why accurate diagnostics are critical. At Sun State International, our technicians are trained to diagnose and repair commercial diesel systems efficiently so you can avoid extended downtime.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-preventing-def",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Preventing DEF System Problems",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "preventing-def"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventing-def-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The best way to avoid major DEF-related repairs is through regular maintenance and proactive inspections. Here are some of the best practices for DEF maintenance:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-preventing-def-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Keep DEF Levels Monitored",
                        "text": "Never ignore low DEF warnings. Refilling early is far easier than dealing with a derated truck on the road."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Use High-Quality DEF",
                        "text": "Poor-quality DEF can contaminate the system and damage components."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Store DEF Properly",
                        "text": "DEF should be stored in temperature-controlled conditions whenever possible to prevent contamination or breakdown."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Schedule Routine Service",
                        "text": "Preventative maintenance allows technicians to inspect emissions systems before small issues become expensive repairs."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-2",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/what-happens-when-you-run-out-of-diesel-exhaust-fluid/2.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
